Revert upstream 70312762 ("CHROMIUM: processor_enable: Fix crash on
ARM64/ARM"). On FydeOS ARM boards there is no ChromeOS firmware flash;
letting the internal programmer proceed past processor detection makes
libflashrom JEDEC-probe physical memory, which latches an asynchronous
SError on rk3588 and panics the kernel (delivered during `futility show`
from update-engine.conf's pre-start, since futility links libflashrom).
Keeping processor detection failing on ARM restores the r144 behavior:
flash access from flashrom/futility aborts harmlessly.

Index: flashrom/processor_enable.c
===================================================================
--- flashrom.orig/processor_enable.c
+++ flashrom/processor_enable.c
@@ -79,10 +79,6 @@ int processor_flash_enable(void)
 	 * FIXME: Move enable_flash_cs5536 and get_flashbase_sc520 here.
 	 */
 	ret = 0;
-#elif defined(__aarch64__) || defined(__arm__)
-	/* ARM and ARM64 processors do not have specific flash enable logic
-	   in this generic helper. */
-	ret = 0;
 #endif
 	return ret;
 }
